    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer planar multilayer stack on CaF2 substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: Layer1=Ge, Layer2=YbF3, Layer3=Ge, Layer4=YbF3, Layer5=Ge, Layer6=YbF3, Layer7=Ge, Layer8=YbF3, Layer9=Ge(defect1), Layer10=YbF3, Layer11=Ge, Layer12=YbF3, Layer13=Ge, Layer14=YbF3, Layer15=Ge, Layer16=YbF3(defect2), Layer17=Ge, Layer18=YbF3, Layer19=Ge, Layer20=YbF3, Layer21=Ge, Layer22=YbF3. All thicknesses bounded [300, 1500] nm. Optimize for: maximize mean transmittance in 3250-3350 nm, maximize mean transmittance in 4200-4300 nm, minimize mean transmittance in 2500-3100 nm, minimize mean transmittance in 4450-5000 nm. Use TMM solver with normal incidence, unpolarized light. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 2500-3100 nm, 3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm, 4450-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands; Low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 24; No metal layers; Conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials only.",
